WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:07.609
Former Republican Senator Jeff flake says
that at least 35 Republican senators would

00:00:07.609 --> 00:00:12.990
vote to remove Donald Trump if the Senate
impeachment vote were private.

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:15.300
So let's back up a little bit.

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:17.890
The entire time I've been talking to you about
impeachment.

00:00:17.890 --> 00:00:23.189
I've been accurately saying, I believe that
as long as Republicans control the Senate,

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:25.369
Trump will not be removed by impeachment.

00:00:25.369 --> 00:00:28.160
The house Democrats can do their impeachment
inquiry.

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:33.300
If it leads them to saying we are filing articles
of impeachment, they can do it, they can do

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:34.560
the impeachment trial.

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:38.730
But no matter what, once it goes to the Republican
controlled Senate, which there will be at

00:00:38.730 --> 00:00:45.890
least until January of 2021 and I believe
until January of 2023 based on the the Senate

00:00:45.890 --> 00:00:51.050
election map, you are not going to remove
Trump because Republicans would not vote to

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:52.850
convict Trump on an impeachment charge.

00:00:52.850 --> 00:00:58.430
Now, I've not mentioned it, but implied in
this is that impeachment votes in the Senate

00:00:58.430 --> 00:01:01.280
are public the way you see senators vote on
stuff.

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:03.340
Yay, nay, a up vote down vote.

00:01:03.340 --> 00:01:07.940
The way they do that, they would publicly
vote on impeachment in that same way.

00:01:07.940 --> 00:01:13.440
But in the back of my mind and that of many
others was the question of imagine that the

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:17.550
Senate impeachment vote was not public, but
instead it was private.

00:01:17.550 --> 00:01:22.030
So at the end of the vote, you would get the
number of senators who voted to impeach and

00:01:22.030 --> 00:01:24.760
the number of senators who voted to acquit.

00:01:24.760 --> 00:01:29.500
Would you have some Republicans who would
be willing to vote for the removal of Donald

00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:31.510
Trump if that's where the evidence brought
them?

00:01:31.510 --> 00:01:36.330
Would Republican senators vote to impeach
Trump if they knew that their vote would not

00:01:36.330 --> 00:01:42.850
be public and therefore they would potentially,
uh, not be subject to the political repercussions

00:01:42.850 --> 00:01:43.850
of it?

00:01:43.850 --> 00:01:47.570
And the growing idea according to a couple
of reports, is that the answer is yes.

00:01:47.570 --> 00:01:53.280
We first heard from Republican political consultant,
Mike Merck, Mike Murphy and Mike Murphy said,

00:01:53.280 --> 00:02:00.940
uh, on MSNBC that if the vote was private,
30 Republican senators would back impeachment.

00:02:00.940 --> 00:02:05.630
Then we heard from former Republican Senator
Jeff flake who said at the Texas Tribune festival

00:02:05.630 --> 00:02:10.990
over the weekend that it's not, or a Thursday,
it was, it's not 30 Republican senators that

00:02:10.990 --> 00:02:12.680
would vote to impeach Trump.

00:02:12.680 --> 00:02:18.150
It's more like at least 35 who would back
impeachment if the impeachment vote were private.

00:02:18.150 --> 00:02:22.500
And because of the balance of power, you actually
don't even need 30 or even 35 Republicans

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:23.810
to get behind impeachment.

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:29.270
You would only need about 20 assuming that
all Democrats and independent senators voted

00:02:29.270 --> 00:02:30.270
for it.

00:02:30.270 --> 00:02:34.720
But this is mostly hypothetical because once
again, it's not a private ballot, it's a public

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:35.720
valid ballot.

00:02:35.720 --> 00:02:38.100
Just like everything that goes on in the Senate.

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:43.230
There's one other element to this, which is
it's not as simple to say if the vote were

00:02:43.230 --> 00:02:50.140
private, 35 Republicans would be in favor
of it because even if the vote were private,

00:02:50.140 --> 00:02:56.070
those Republican senators who voted against
impeachment would come out and say afterwards,

00:02:56.070 --> 00:02:58.970
even if it's a private vote, I voted against
impeachment.

00:02:58.970 --> 00:03:04.160
And this would immediately put the spotlight
on the Republicans that don't come forward

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:09.800
and say, I voted against a convicting, and
they would either have to lie or admit it.

00:03:09.800 --> 00:03:13.800
So it's sort of a fantasy that it would even
go down in this way.

00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:18.599
But what this signals then is a huge cowardice
on the part of the Republicans because if

00:03:18.599 --> 00:03:23.030
it's true that they're only willing to vote
to impeach if the vote is secret and it doesn't

00:03:23.030 --> 00:03:27.420
have political ramifications for them, it's
merely a political calculation.

00:03:27.420 --> 00:03:33.700
Now, the upside if we want to find a silver
lining here is that I guess they're not all

00:03:33.700 --> 00:03:36.120
blindly loyal to Donald Trump.

00:03:36.120 --> 00:03:40.150
The downside is they're afraid to act on it
unless it's done in a way that it will have

00:03:40.150 --> 00:03:41.709
no consequences whatsoever.

00:03:41.709 --> 00:03:47.380
I read a comment online when researching the
story that sums it up as they're not all traders.

00:03:47.380 --> 00:03:51.870
Some merely have no integrity and it, it's
not even just lack of integrity.

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:57.650
There's also the issue of hypocrisy because
in addition to the lack of lacking integrity,

00:03:57.650 --> 00:04:01.870
they would instantly be voting to impeach
a democratic president who had done all of

00:04:01.870 --> 00:04:03.879
the things that Donald Trump has done.

00:04:03.879 --> 00:04:06.910
This may not even be a decision they end up
having to make.

00:04:06.910 --> 00:04:11.870
We're just at the beginning of the inquiry,
which happens before articles are filed, which

00:04:11.870 --> 00:04:15.099
would happen before all of the other things
that we've discussed.

00:04:15.099 --> 00:04:22.940
But if Jeff flake is only 20% correct, if,
uh, Mike Murphy is only 30% correct, that

00:04:22.940 --> 00:04:27.919
means that there would be the desire from
enough Republicans in the Senate to impeach

00:04:27.919 --> 00:04:29.949
that it could remove Donald Trump.

00:04:29.949 --> 00:04:31.880
But Mark my words, you are not

00:04:31.880 --> 00:04:35.889
going to see it under this current Republican
controlled set.

00:04:35.889 --> 00:04:36.889
Let's take a break.

00:04:36.889 --> 00:04:37.669
We will be back with much more right after
this

